WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.640
Welcome to Grade 1 English, Unit 8: Wonderful Water.

2
00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:06.780
In this unit you will learn about water.

3
00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:09.900
You will learn where it comes from and where we find it.

4
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.540
You will learn all the ways we use it every day.

5
00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:14.860
You will meet rainy and sunny weather.

6
00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:17.060
You will meet animals that live in water.

7
00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:20.060
Water is a gift, and we should never waste it.

8
00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:21.960
Say the words out loud.

9
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.720
This is about confident English and being
thankful for water, not perfect spelling.

10
00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:32.820
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

11
00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:39.260
By the end of this unit, you will be able to say
why plants, animals, and people all need water.

12
00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:44.660
You will also name places where we
find water (rain, river, sea, well).

13
00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:49.780
You will also say how we use water:
“I use water to drink / wash / cook.”

14
00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:52.240
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

15
00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:59.040
Your vocabulary work begins with these
words: duck, sock, clock, queen, quick, quiz.

16
00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:04.540
Listen to each word, look at what it means,
and try to use it when you talk and write.

17
00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:10.120
The reading sequence includes The Well in
the Village and Talk about Wonderful Water.

18
00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:15.680
Read slowly, look at the pictures,
and find the big idea in each text.

19
00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:20.040
When you answer a question, point to the words that show it.

20
00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:24.480
The first language focus is Say what you use water for.

21
00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:27.200
Think of one way you use water every day.

22
00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:30.540
After 'to', use the plain action word.

23
00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:34.740
Look at the examples, then try
the pattern in your own sentences.

24
00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:38.740
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 - Listen and point.

25
00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:41.720
Say your ideas clearly and listen to your partner.

26
00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:47.250
In writing, you will draw, trace, copy or write,
then check your work with a grown-up or the AI tutor.

27
00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:48.940
You are ready to begin.

28
00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:53.960
Start with the words, then the reading and the
questions, then the grammar, speaking and writing.

29
00:01:54.680 --> 00:02:00.240
Ask the AI tutor for help any time, and bring your
questions to a live session too if you join one.
